<p>UK health officials are investigating 27 meningitis-related cases linked to an outbreak centered on the University of Kent in Canterbury and Club Chemistry, a local nightclub popular with students. So far, 15 laboratory cases have been confirmed, and officials are investigating 12 further notifications. Two young people have died. In response, the University of Kent started a targeted meningitis B vaccination campaign for about 5,000 students. Officials also urged anyone who attended Club Chemistry in Canterbury on March 5, 6 or 7 to come forward for antibiotics.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/IAfh5xwt1VrjILkYPzvZhtuG6v7YB-JFL1_4HlpjaQI29gK4uy9Bk2zuLNSLzV5plTC1PTEVKeImazZetIoMiHBvAfZIQ2F5gzJxFiL_ohRj' alt='People queue to receive vaccinations at the sports centre on the University of Kent campus following the outbreak in Canterbury, Britain, on March 18, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Beyond the Canterbury campus: Although the outbreak is centered on the University of Kent and a student nightclub in Canterbury, one of the two deaths was a teenage student at a school in Faversham, showing the cluster was not confined to a single university community.</li><li>A clue in the strain: Six of the nine confirmed cases cited earlier in the week were group B meningococcal infections, the strain behind the university&#x27;s targeted MenB vaccination effort.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK Health Security Agency: A British health official said it was too soon to say the Kent outbreak had been contained after authorities reported seven new cases, a sign that active monitoring was still under way. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/british-health-official-says-too-soon-to-declare-kent-meningitis-outbreak-contained'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Prime Minister Keir Starmer: Starmer told parliament that health experts were working to identify close contacts of those who were ill, alongside the public appeal to recent nightclub attendees. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>University of Kent: Hundreds of students queued on campus on Wednesday after the university opened a targeted MenB vaccination programme, making the campus the hub of the response. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/health/article/2026/03/19/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-at-least-27_6751605_14.html'>UK meningitis outbreak cases rise to at least 27</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/19/falklands-concerns-on-the-meningitis-b-outbreak-in-uk-islands-children-have-been-vaccinated-since-2025'>Falklands, concerns on the Meningitis B outbreak in UK; Islands’ children have been vaccinated since 2025</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/18/world/europe/uk-meningitis-outbreak-kent-symptoms-vaccine.html'>As a Meningitis Outbreak Spreads in Kent, UK, Here’s What to Know</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983724/uk-meningitis-outbreak-cases-rise-to-27'>UK meningitis outbreak cases rise to 27</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3347095/unprecedented-spread-uk-races-contain-deadly-meningitis-outbreak'>‘Unprecedented in spread’: UK races to contain deadly meningitis outbreak</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/british-health-official-says-too-soon-to-declare-kent-meningitis-outbreak-contained'>British health official says too soon to declare Kent meningitis outbreak contained</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>